After playing around a lot, I noticed the INT/CHR thing too.  I also had a
pretty good idea of which actions were good and which were bad.  Being curious
as to the implementation, I checked out the source.

Yes, different actions (MANY different actions) affect your stats.  Dragging
around an iron ball would certainly help out your physical stats.  All
"learning" related things go into wisdom, however - INT and CHA don't get
exercised.

All in all, the details are what you'd expect - exercise, eat well - your
physical stats go up.  Learn things, your wisdom goes up.  Do tricky things,
your dex gets better.  The converse of all the above is true too - ie, do
clumsy things and your dex goes down.

Perhaps a better way of phrasing it - the actions give you modifiers to the
periodic rolls that check for stat gain/loss.

